#hasheq((content-digest . "093483517ecdda6ec04ca983f4dafc6fa9df261fa882fc552ef65aa9c6fbb801") (findings . ("1. (minor, non-blocking) The idempotency constraint's restart clause (a restart mid-pass re-runs safely and converges) is proven only for the same-port repeat pass; the github-port journal is in-memory and issue-close/board-set-field have no adapter-level external dedup, so a fresh port after a real process restart would re-issue both commands with the same deterministic correlation ids. Convergence then relies on server-side idempotency (closing a closed issue, setting the same field value), which no test at this head witnesses. The base test covering restart covers only id determinism." "2. (minor, non-blocking) The check-true (andmap gsd-github-command-result-already-done? ...) assertion is vacuously true on an empty action list; unreachable here because a 'reconciled result always contains at least the issue-close action, but a future refactor could silently weaken it." "3. (observation) Historical waves are skipped via the uniform fail-closed 'blocked status with a recorded reason rather than a distinct 'skipped status; all observable skip requirements (no exception, no tracker effect, no state flip, wave stays 'done) are directly asserted, so this is a naming nuance, not a constraint violation." "4. (provenance, non-blocking) The v1.00.33-w0 gate-capture artifacts (incl. SHA256SUMS) are not present in this checkout; they were authored on origin/main after the branch point via #9812/#9813 and reference merge head a553e457. The in-checkout diff (tests + README only) is consistent with the frozen wave claim; independent confirmation of the six gates relies on those main-side captures.")) (report . "The two regression cases genuinely prove the frozen constraints, not vacuously. The idempotency witness routes the op-counting fake adapter through the REAL github port with dry-run off, so correlation-id journal replay is production-enforced: a repeat pass yields 'reconciled with adapter counts still exactly 1/1 and every result already-done?=#t (a flag only the journal-replay path sets), and any replay regression would show counts of 2 and fail. The historical-skip witness proves fail-closed semantics: a done wave with no receipt/journal/handoff is refused ('blocked, empty actions, zero logged port executions even though the injected delivery reader would have said delivered), and the reloaded record stays 'done - the reconciliation module provably contains no campaign-state writes, so no wave can be flipped or mutated without full receipt/handoff/readback proof. Direction of truth is one-way everywhere I looked; nothing in the diff touches production code. Weaknesses are minor (see findings): restart-mid-pass convergence across a genuinely NEW port is not directly witnessed, the andmap already-done? check is vacuous on an empty list (unreachable for status 'reconciled since the close action is always appended), and the skip is surfaced as 'blocked-with-reason rather than a distinct 'skipped status - an acceptable naming choice since every observable requirement of skipped-not-failed is directly asserted. README metrics verified as an exact pure regeneration (lint green, +61 lines / +11 assertions match numstat and hand-count). None of these weaknesses undermines a constraint, so the verdict is APPROVED.") (reviewed-sha . "a553e45784351468781c1aa6494116ec96486c22") (reviewer . "independent code reviewer, fresh-context pi reviewer agent (zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3), campaign 79a69b42 W0") (scope . "I read the two new test cases in tests/test-gsd-tracker-reconciliation.rkt plus every helper and production module they exercise (tests/helpers/gsd-port-fakes.rkt, extensions/gsd/tracker-reconciliation.rkt, extensions/gsd/github-port.rkt, extensions/gsd/tracker-production-wiring.rkt, effect-ports.rkt), verified the wave diff against the merge-base (exactly the test file 62+/1- and README 2+/2-), ran the focused test file at this head (8/8 pass) and the metrics lint, and inspected the head merge topology and the v1.00.33-w0 gate-capture provenance on origin/main.") (timestamp . "2026-10-08T10:58:00Z") (verdict . "APPROVED"))
